<title>BRAZIL: ACPC cuts may include Brazil robustas - Ugandan min.</title>
<headline>ACPC cuts may include Brazil robustas - Ugandan min.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A 1.5-million bag proposed cut in arabica producer exports may also include a reduction in robusta exports by top producer Brazil, said Uganda's Trade and Industry Minister.</p>
<p>African nations will on January 23 present a plan to reduce exports by the members of the Association of Coffee Producing Countries (ACPC) by a total of 2.5 million bags in the first half of this year.</p>
<p>Earlier Uganda's Abel Rwendeire said the 2.5 million bags would involve one million bags of robusta exports but he later said there may be additional reductions in robusta exports from Brazil, regarded principally as an arabica coffee producer.</p>
<p>--Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom +55 21 507 4151</p>
